  "notes": "Ichidan (ru-verb): {経|へ}る → {経|へ}ない → {経|へ}た → {経|へ}て.\n\nUSAGE:\nThe te-form {経|へ}て is extremely common, meaning \"after going through\" or \"via.\" It is used both for physical routes ({大阪|おおさか}を{経|へ}て) and abstract processes ({審査|しんさ}を{経|へ}て). For the time sense, it is often literary or formal.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {通|とお}る: to pass through (physical movement)\n- {過|す}ぎる: to pass, to go by (of time)\n- {経過|けいか}する: to elapse, to pass (noun/verb-suru form)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- 〜を{経|へ}て: via, after going through\n- {時|とき}を{経|へ}る: time passes\n- {年月|ねんげつ}を{経|へ}る: years pass\n- {過程|かてい}を{経|へ}る: go through a process",
